2. How do map(), filter(), and reduce() work in streams? Can you give a real-world example combining them?

| Method     | Purpose                             | Example                                        |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| `map()`    | Transforms elements                 | `list.stream().map(String::toUpperCase)`       |
| `filter()` | Selects elements matching predicate | `list.stream().filter(s -> s.startsWith("A"))` |
| `reduce()` | Aggregates into a single result     | `list.stream().reduce("", (a,b) -> a+b)`       |

List<String> names = List.of("Alice","Bob","Anita","Alex");
String result = names.stream()
                     .filter(n -> n.startsWith("A"))
                     .map(String::toUpperCase)
                     .reduce("", (a,b) -> a + b);
System.out.println(result); // ALICEANITALEX


