3. Difference between Stream and ParallelStream. When would you not use parallel streams?

stream() → sequential processing on a single thread.

parallelStream() → splits work into multiple threads (ForkJoinPool).


When not to use parallel:

For small data sets (thread overhead > gain).

When operations are stateful or dependent.

When the source isn’t efficiently splittable (e.g., I/O streams).

✅ Lead insight: Use parallel only for CPU-intensive, stateless, independent operations on large collections.

