7. Can you explain how default and static methods in interfaces help in backward compatibility?

Introduced for backward compatibility — to add new behavior without breaking existing implementations.

Default method:
interface Vehicle {
    default void start() { System.out.println("Vehicle starting..."); }
}

Static method:
interface Vehicle {
    static void info() { System.out.println("Static info"); }
}



