8. What is method reference? When is it preferable over lambda?

A concise shorthand for a lambda that calls an existing method.

| Type        | Example               |
| ----------- | --------------------- |
| Static      | `Math::max`           |
| Instance    | `System.out::println` |
| Constructor | `ArrayList::new`      |

List<String> names = List.of("a","b","c");
names.forEach(System.out::println);

Method references improve readability, especially in stream chains—prefer them when the lambda simply delegates to another method.

usage of method reference:
| Type                                       | Example               | Equivalent Lambda            |
| ------------------------------------------ | --------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| 1️⃣ **Object::instanceMethod**             | `System.out::println` | `x -> System.out.println(x)` |
| 2️⃣ **Class::staticMethod**                | `Math::max`           | `(a, b) -> Math.max(a, b)`   |
| 3️⃣ **Class::instanceMethod**              | `String::toUpperCase` | `s -> s.toUpperCase()`       |
| 4️⃣ **ClassName::new** *(constructor ref)* | `ArrayList::new`      | `() -> new ArrayList<>()`    |
